W: 2. He takes his pick an doon he goes
W: To hew the coal that lies below.
W: But there's not a woman in this town row
W: Would look at a blackleg miner.
W:
W: 3. Oh, Delaval is a terrible place,
W: They rub wet clay in the blackleg's face.
W: Around the pit-heaps they run a foot race
W: To catch the blackleg miner.
W:
W: 4. Divvn't gan near the Seghill mine
W: Across the way they stretch a line
W: To catch the throat an break the spine
W: Of the dirty blackleg miner
W:
W: 5. Tak your tools an gear as well
W: An hoy them doon the pit of hell.
W: Doon ye go an fare ye well
W: Ye dirty blackleg miner.
W:
W: 6. So join the union while ye may.
W: Don't wait 'til your dying day.
W: For that may not be far away,
W: Ye dirty blackleg miner.
